{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183072-compromise-queries","id":183072,"title":"Compromise Queries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-28T11:09:53-07:00","id":183072,"title":"Compromise Queries","content":"I apologize if these have already been addressed, scoured most of the forum off and on for various things but i don't believe anything quite addressed some of my concerns. This goes specifically to the issues of acting out of cover (OOC, here)<br /> <br /> Are you invoking a compromise roll if...<br /> <br /> 1. you are wearing a disguise or a mask and commit a crime (and your cover isn't criminal)<br /> 2. you take an OOC action with your cover and no one is there to see it (i.e., you pick a lock and your cover is a suburban housewife with 0 larceny)<br /> 3. you take an OOC action against someone who has no idea who you are (and through the course of events, never will)<br /> 4. you do something OOC against a supernatural who already knows you aren't human<br /> 5. you take an OOC action around someone who already knows what you are (in this case, something mundane and not supernatural, like string theory from a 10 year old whose life is sports)<br /> <br /> Basically, any other actions along these lines as well. I guess what i'm also getting at is, is incorporating temporary covers into your existence THAT necessary just to avoid these for a quick action against a location/collection mission. Hell, there's another example, trusting soccer mom performing a stakeout against a person.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3363-viridian-sun","name":"viridian sun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T14:36:18-07:00","id":183231,"title":"","content":"So, all of these questions are kind of along the same lines: Where are the dividing lines for what constitutes an &quot;out of character action&quot; for a given Cover, WRT a compromise?<br /> <br /> Like a lot of things, it's not black and white. But the principles I go by when running <b>Demon </b>are:<br /> <br /> 1) <i>Is the compromise roll going to detract from the story? </i>I never make the players roll just to make them roll, but with that said, the Storytelling system works when you use it. Rolls can generate Beats, and so on. So if the compromise roll is just going to be a distraction, I'll let it slide. If it's something minor (#2 in your examples) I'll let it slide. <br /> <br /> 2) <i>Do the circumstances indicate the God-Machine has a decent chance of noticing?</i> That is, are there cameras? Is there a crowd, with people using phones? Is someone likely to get on Facebook later and say &quot;You know, I saw something weird earlier...&quot; even if they think no more of it? If the character is alone, it's less of a problem. Covers have a good deal of flexibility because people do. But...<br /> <br /> 3) <i>Is the supernatural involved?</i> It follows that the God-Machine watches out for supernatural activity, because it figures that demons would be more lax around other supernatural beings. So in #4, I'd probably call for the roll. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T15:32:11-07:00","id":183278,"title":"","content":"The clarification is much appreciated. I've been long looking for ya'll to push out a NWoD Demon, and am about to kick off my first such campaign this weekend. I've been trying to affirm how much of it is &quot;psychic paper&quot; (and thus any activity angers &quot;god,&quot; a-la paradox and mage) and how much of it is just being caught in the act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3363-viridian-sun","name":"viridian sun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}